+
+/// Whether one sync now could change `decide`'s answer: for a binding that is on, when the list
+/// cannot decide (should_refresh_for). Neither a sync nor anything else but a login on this PC
+/// turns a binding on.
+fn wants_sync(view: &View, outcome: &Result<KeyEntry, Refusal>, now: u64, key_serial: u64) -> bool {
+    view.binding.is_some()
+        && !view.off
+        && should_refresh_for(outcome, view.cached.as_ref(), now, key_serial)
